What is derived from tbaMUD
---------------------------

- **`content/`** — the world and game data. Every `*.yaml` file is converted by
  `tools/tbaport` from the tbaMUD world files (`lib/world/**`), the tbaMUD
  text and message files (`lib/text/*`, `lib/misc/messages`), and the DG Script
  trigger records (`*.trg`). Area designs, room/mob/object descriptions and
  scripts are the work of their original tbaMUD authors, credited in the source
  files and in the converted content.
- **`crates/dg-vm/`** — a line-faithful Rust port of tbaMUD's DG Scripts
  interpreter (`tbamud/src/dg_*.c`, `dg_scripts.c`, `dg_triggers.c`,
  `dg_mobcmd.c`, `dg_objcmd.c`, `dg_variables.c`). The port is the authors'
  original Rust expression, but it is a derivative work of that C source and is
  subject to the same terms.
- **`reports/`** and parts of **`docs/`** — describe and summarise that
  converted content.

The Rust engine glue (the `mib-tba` crate in `code/`, the `dg-vm` host
implementation, and the `tbaport` converter itself) is original code under the
MIT licence in [`LICENSE`](LICENSE). The MIT licence does not apply to the
tbaMUD-derived material above.

