Obligations when running the game
---------------------------------

The CircleMUD licence additionally requires a running derivative to:

1. show the credit text for the in-game **`credits` command**. The engine owns
   that command and aggregates every loaded pack's `stdlib.credits` section
   (MIB issue #22), so this pack ships
   [`content/stdlib.credits.yaml`](content/stdlib.credits.yaml) alongside the
   base stdlib pack's; the converted tbaMUD `lib/text/credits` text is also
   preserved as the `credits` help topic in `content/stdlib.help.yaml`;
2. maintain the **`CIRCLEMUD` help entry** intact and display it for
   `help circlemud`: the converter preserves it as the `circlemud` help topic
   (see `docs/05-converter.md` §3.8); and
3. include the **names of the DikuMUD and CircleMUD creators in the login
   sequence**: the pack's server binary sets a default `game.motd` naming them.

Upstream tbaMUD sources for the credit texts: `lib/text/credits`,
`lib/text/help/help.hlp` (`CIRCLEMUD`), and `lib/text/greetings`.

Do not remove, change or modify any notice of copyright, licensing or
authorship found in tbaMUD-derived material.
